# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Understanding what the patient said: Google Gemini
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey  (starts with AIza)
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# There is deliberately nothing else to set here.
#
# The model is gemini-3-flash-preview and the temperature is 0, both PINNED in lib/llm.ts
# rather than read from the environment. On a medical form the same reply has to fill the
# same fields every time or the output cannot be audited, and "which model read this
# patient's words" should have one answer you can read off the source instead of one that
# depends on a deployment's env vars. tests/llm.test.ts asserts that setting GEMINI_MODEL
# or GEMINI_TEMPERATURE changes nothing.
#
# Extraction ran on Anthropic's claude-haiku-4-5 before this, chosen the same way and
# pinned for the same reasons. It moved because the key stopped authenticating - a hard
# 401, which no amount of code can retry its way out of. The model was then probed rather
# than trusted: temperature 0 accepted, bare JSON via responseMimeType, the Hinglish probe
# correct ("din mein 6-7 ho jaati hai" to "Moderate 5-10/day"), 2.8s for a full habits
# slice, and 69/69 fields on the fixture eval.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Turning speech into words: Sarvam (Saaras)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://dashboard.sarvam.ai
#
# This is the one thing the model cannot do: neither Gemini's text endpoint nor Anthropic's
# takes audio here, so something has to turn a recording into words before a model can read
# them. That is all this key is for. It produces a string, the string is shown to the
# patient, and every decision about the ANSWER is still the model's.
#
# Sarvam is the locally-right pick: saaras is trained on Indian-accented English and
# Hinglish, and mode=codemix returns mixed Hindi/English in Roman script, which is also
# the easiest thing for the extraction step to read.
#
# Leaving this unset does not break anything. /api/transcribe answers 503, the microphone
# says once that it is not set up here and stops offering itself, and every question is
# still answerable by tapping.
SARVAM_API_KEY=
SARVAM_MODEL=saaras:v3
SARVAM_MODE=codemix

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reading the question out loud
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No key, and nothing to configure. The read-aloud button speaks through the browser's own
# speechSynthesis. Free, offline, instant, and no audio of a patient's answers ever leaves
# the device.
